18:T5e5,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How is the Germany blocked account amount calculated?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"For a standard calculation, multiply the current monthly requirement by the number of required months. Any scholarship reduction must be accepted by the responsible visa authority."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is the blocked-account deposit an extra cost?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. It remains the applicant's money and is released in restricted monthly amounts after arrival, although provider and transfer fees are separate costs."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can a scholarship reduce the blocked amount?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A recognised scholarship can be accepted as financial proof, but the responsible mission decides whether the specific award covers all or part of the requirement."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does the calculator guarantee a student visa?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. It is a planning tool. The German mission assesses the official documents, current financial requirement and complete visa application."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why can real monthly costs be higher than the official amount?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The official amount is a standard financial threshold. Actual rent, deposits, insurance, university charges and lifestyle depend on the applicant's location and circumstances."}}]}1:["$","main",null,{"id":"main-content","className":"editorial-page editorial-page--tool","children":[[["$","script","0",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"WebPage\",\"@id\":\"https://aspirecompass.org/tools/germany-blocked-account-calculator/\",\"name\":\"Germany blocked account amount and student cost calculator\",\"description\":\"Estimate a Germany blocked-account deposit and first-year study bu